# nr-office-ooxml-xlsx-charts-soffice: mixdog-ooxml gains xlsx_charts (add_chart, chart cache refresh) and soffice (the LibreOffice driver).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/src/lib.rs

Module lines: add after `pub mod xlsx_assertions;`:

    pub mod soffice;
    pub mod xlsx_charts;

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/Cargo.toml

Add a new table after `[dependencies]` (before `[dev-dependencies]`). The job object that stops LibreOffice's process tree on Windows is
written in soffice/run.rs (same calls as mixdog-exthost/src/containment.rs; that crate is not a dependency). Win32_System_Threading is used
by tests/soffice_lifecycle.rs to ask whether a process is still running:

    [target.'cfg(windows)'.dependencies]
    windows-sys = { workspace = true, features = [
        "Win32_Foundation",
        "Win32_Security",
        "Win32_System_JobObjects",
        "Win32_System_Threading",
    ] }

No other new dependency: mixdog-fonts (Os, HostEnv, mac_office_font_dir), mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js, mixdog-rt (time), reqwest (Url::from_file_path),
tokio (features rt, time, net, process, io-util: already listed), uuid (v4) and tempfile (dev) are in the list already.

## native/core/Cargo.lock

mixdog-ooxml gains the dependency `windows-sys` (already locked, one version). `cargo update -w` offline writes it.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

Run the repository's hakari check after the edge above; take its output if it asks for a feature of windows-sys.

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json

Index entry for the new set (the set's own MANIFEST.json is in the worktree under native/core/fixtures/office-xlsx-charts-soffice/; the digest below is of
that file as committed). Add to "sets", in name order:

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-xlsx-charts-soffice.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-xlsx-charts-soffice/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "82e9bf144daeb4d713dbafdc25b072525f91bc9573f69ce37bcbd26a6ede80a3",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-xlsx-charts-soffice.mjs",
      "set": "office-xlsx-charts-soffice",
      "totalBytes": 641509
    }

The recording was made from a scratch checkout whose git history is not the product's (the recorder was run with `--tree C:/Project/mixdog` and
the recorders' lib copied beside it), so the manifest's `product.commit` is null and `refComparison.closestCommit` names that scratch commit. Re-record
once from the integration checkout (`node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-xlsx-charts-soffice.mjs --tree <Node product tree>`): golden.json
does not change, the manifest's identity does; then update the digest above.

## What the callers must do (interfaces added)

- `mixdog_ooxml::xlsx_charts::add_worksheet_chart(measurer, zip, sheet, xml, op, sheets)` is the add_chart operation: the xlsx operation dispatcher
  (the task that ports the operation table of portable-xlsx.mjs) calls it with `sheets = workbook_sheets(zip)` and the operation's JSON.
  `refresh_chart_caches(zip)` is called by the driver after a recalculation; nothing else needs to call it.
- `mixdog_ooxml::soffice::Soffice` is the driver (`Soffice::process()` for the process-wide one: one private profile and one queue). Its calls take the
  job's write proof and block; a cancellation is the `AtomicBool` the caller sets: `available()`, `render(proof, path, output, RenderFormat::{Pdf,Png}, cancel)`,
  `recalculate_workbook(proof, path, force, cancel)`, `validate_reopen(proof, path, cancel)`, `convert_legacy_office(proof, path, output, cancel, hooks)`.
  The reports are the JSON the Node functions answered, key for key.
- The process must call `Soffice::process().shutdown(proof)` as it ends (the private profile is removed there; Node did it from a process exit handler,
  which Rust has no equivalent of). The place is the daemon's shutdown path of whichever task wires the office engine.

## SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs)

No name to remove: this task registers no service.
